WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.201
The Moon over you tonight.

00:02.901 --> 00:05.841
This is the Moon from your own ground tonight.

00:06.291 --> 00:10.811
The lit side always points at the Sun, even when the Sun has set.

00:11.261 --> 00:17.715
Look again tomorrow at the same hour: it will be a little further east, and a little different in shape.
